2 CONT
2 CONT Olava Martine Minge died right after giving birth twins on January 20, 1886. Her twins survived. Her baby daughter, who was her namesake, Olava Martine Minge was born on January 20, 1886 and died died when she was 8 weeks old on M
2 CONC arch 13, 1886. Her baby son, Carl August Minge was born on January 19, 1886 and he lived to be 66 years old when he died on December 3, 1952. After Olava died, her husband Martin began using her last name Minge since her family wa
2 CONC s helping to raise their children.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family used the last name of her husband, Hans  Martin Eskildsen, when they lived in Norway. When they immigrated to America they used the last name Ryen (Hans Martin Eskildsen lived on the Ryen farm in Norway). Then they chan
2 CONC ged their last name to Minge (Olava's family was from the Minge farm in Norway in Tune, Ostfold).
