1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://www.digitalarkivet.no/kb20061023010089 Vielsen 1826] Enke
2 CONT [https://www.digitalarkivet.no/view/327/pv00000009019291 Vielsen 1826]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Karen Andersdatter Biørnland Ødegaard was born December 1771 on Biørnland Ødegaard, Tune, Østfold, Norway and was baptized December 29, 1771 in Tune kirke. Her name is later listed as Kari.  Her parents were Anders Busen (Bueson) 
2 CONC and Marthe Madsdatter Biørnland Ødegaard under Holleby., and Johanne Torbiørnsdatter Biørnland, Siri Madsdatter Biørnland, Johanes Brevig, Helge Askutsen Radet, and Ole Olsen Biørnland were witnesses at her baptism.
2 CONT
2 CONT She got engagement to marry Magnus Halvorsen Røed on December 29, 1797, and they got married February 13, 1798 in Tune kirke witnessed by Ole Jensen Strøm and Mons Andersen Brække.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kari died January 25, 1842 and was buried January 30, 1842 at Tune kirke. She lived at Bjørnlandhytta. (At the time of her death, she was listed as a widow after Magnus Halvorsen’s death, but re- married to Nils Olsen)            
2 CONC
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Gift 1. gang 13. feb. 1798 med Magnus Halvorsen fra Rød. Han døde 25. jan. 1821 på Holen, Tune. Gravlagt 4. feb. SAO, Tune prestekontor Kirkebøker, F/Fa/L0004: Ministerialbok nr. 4, 1797-1815, s. 345-346. <http://urn.digitalarkive
